The dynamic `import()` calls are failing the TypeScript strict type checking because `tsc -b` (project build mode) doesn't use the same path resolution as Vite. The vite config has the alias:
```ts
resolve: {
  alias: {
    "knirvwallet-module": path.resolve(__dirname, "./core/packages/knirvwallet-module/src"),
  },
},
```

But this is a Vite-specific resolve alias. The `tsc -b` command uses the tsconfig paths instead. Let me check the tsconfig files.

Actually, the original code had `// @ts-ignore` comments for the static import. When I changed to dynamic import, the `// @ts-ignore` might not work the same way. Let me check the tsconfig.

